description:
pkix-revocation/src/crl.rs:19–22

    /// OID for CRLNumber extension (RFC 5280 §5.2.3) — id-ce-cRLNumber: 2.5.29.20
    #[allow(dead_code)]
    const OID_CRL_NUMBER: der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier =
        der::asn1::ObjectIdentifier::new_unwrap("2.5.29.20");

OID_CRL_NUMBER is used at line 338 (crl_number() function: 'e.extn_id == OID_CRL_NUMBER').  The #[allow(dead_code)] attribute is stale — clippy would not warn about this constant without it.

Additionally, crl_number() itself carries #[allow(dead_code)] at line 317:

    #[allow(dead_code)]
    fn uint_to_u64(n: &der::asn1::Uint) -> Option<u64> { ... }

The function is called by both crl_number() and base_crl_number(), which are both called from with_delta() — the allow is also stale here.

Remove the stale allow(dead_code) attributes from OID_CRL_NUMBER and uint_to_u64.
